WEBVTT

00:02.461 --> 00:06.571
Why don't we all search the 
archive for Reid's book?

00:06.571 --> 00:13.791
You're talking about using Reid's book
as a guide to defeating him, I suppose?

00:14.101 --> 00:15.241
Yeah.

00:15.241 --> 00:18.131
If we read his book of the dead, 
we'll find out how he died.

00:18.641 --> 00:20.761
He's no exception to the rule.

00:20.761 --> 00:22.511
When you put it that way, it makes sense.

00:22.511 --> 00:24.541
Not the proper way,
but the unorthodox way.

00:24.541 --> 00:26.331
That suits you, Barusu.

00:26.331 --> 00:27.601
Yes, it does.

00:28.161 --> 00:31.261
Subaru is very good at 
that sort of hoodwinking.

00:31.261 --> 00:34.251
Another word you don't hear 
in this day and age...

00:34.251 --> 00:40.861
But can we be certain that 
Reid Astrea's book is in the archive?

00:40.861 --> 00:45.001
There is no doubt that 
he lived 400 years ago.

00:45.311 --> 00:49.471
But there's no way he's been 
alive for 400 years, right?

00:49.471 --> 00:50.801
He's gotta be dead.

00:50.801 --> 00:52.871
You can't be sure of that.

00:53.341 --> 00:56.581
Despite appearances, Betty has been 
alive for 400 years, I suppose.

00:56.581 --> 00:59.421
I think I've been alive 
for about 100 years, too.

00:59.761 --> 01:03.551
It's about 400 for me, too, in terms 
of years since I came into being.

01:03.551 --> 01:06.881
And I've been waiting
around for 400 years.

01:06.881 --> 01:09.201
We've got a lot of long-lived 
characters here!

01:09.201 --> 01:10.631
Even you, Emilia-chan?!

01:12.201 --> 01:15.191
That said, given his personality,

01:15.191 --> 01:17.281
I doubt he is of a long-lived species.

01:17.281 --> 01:21.661
His personality? You mean... 
how he's really lively?

01:22.021 --> 01:25.411
Not so much lively
as uninhibited, perhaps.

01:26.401 --> 01:28.471
Even if he is of a long-lived species,

01:28.471 --> 01:32.601
I find it hard to believe he'd spend 400
years sitting around in this tower.

01:32.601 --> 01:33.331
Good point.

01:34.101 --> 01:36.721
When I think about who Reid Astrea is,

01:36.721 --> 01:40.381
he doesn't strike me as a man 
who'd stay in one place for long.

01:42.091 --> 01:46.591
So are we in agreement that 
Reid is a very lively dead man?

01:48.631 --> 01:49.301
Well, then...

01:50.531 --> 01:53.141
If that's what it takes to 
clear the tower, then...

01:53.991 --> 01:55.021
let's do it!

02:04.831 --> 02:07.281
What's wrong? Still not down for this?

02:07.671 --> 02:10.611
No, there is no other way out.

02:10.611 --> 02:13.461
I acknowledge that your idea is valid.

02:13.851 --> 02:15.981
But you have your doubts about it?

02:17.461 --> 02:20.431
This is my own problem.

02:20.431 --> 02:22.001
Please don't worry about it.

02:24.451 --> 02:25.211
Ram!

02:27.171 --> 02:29.301
Can you look out for the others for a bit?

02:34.411 --> 02:36.811
So what did you wish to discuss with me?

02:39.101 --> 02:41.521
Do you have any
intention of defeating Reid?

02:44.301 --> 02:46.511
Subaru, you...

02:46.511 --> 02:50.401
Sorry. The truth is, I'd like to 
spend as much time as I have to

02:50.401 --> 02:53.451
getting your wounded heart fixed up.

02:54.041 --> 02:56.041
But we don't have time for that.

02:56.511 --> 02:58.751
So I'll be straight with you, Julius.

03:01.931 --> 03:02.781
Let's hear it.

03:03.681 --> 03:06.481
That's one thing. This is something else.

03:06.481 --> 03:07.421
Huh?

03:08.001 --> 03:11.901
I get why you feel uncomfortable 
when you look at me.

03:11.901 --> 03:15.791
The Subaru I was before yesterday 
must've done something to you.

03:15.791 --> 03:19.091
But that has nothing to do
with who I am now.

03:20.601 --> 03:24.841
You're the strongest one in our party.

03:24.841 --> 03:28.461
So even if we find the perfect 
strategy guide to conquering him,

03:28.461 --> 03:31.341
we'll still need you to 
be the one to fight him.

03:32.011 --> 03:35.231
I have already lost to him twice.

03:35.231 --> 03:36.381
I know.

03:38.331 --> 03:40.721
But you can win next time.

03:41.791 --> 03:43.721
I didn't see how it ended.

03:43.721 --> 03:46.441
I don't even remember 
anything before yesterday.

03:46.441 --> 03:47.381
So...

03:47.761 --> 03:51.721
I have no knowledge of 
you ever losing to Reid.

03:53.291 --> 03:55.391
What you're lacking isn't courage.

03:58.771 --> 04:01.811
It's the will to win—the 
determination not to lose.

04:01.811 --> 04:05.061
You've got all the courage 
you need right here.

04:06.111 --> 04:09.671
I'll be leaving Reid Astrea to you.

04:09.671 --> 04:12.621
You should be the one to take 
down our most challenging enemy.

04:15.871 --> 04:20.751
How can you expect so much of me when 
you remember nothing before yesterday?

04:21.461 --> 04:26.141
It's just, you know... the way I see you.

04:26.811 --> 04:29.211
Everything about you gives me that hope.

04:31.011 --> 04:31.921
I see.

04:33.061 --> 04:35.641
So my appearance made you feel that way.

04:36.951 --> 04:42.691
Even forgotten by the world and unable 
to confirm my master's existence,

04:42.691 --> 04:46.481
it isn't as if I've lost everything 
I cultivated over my life.

04:47.021 --> 04:48.561
That's what you mean, isn't it?

04:48.561 --> 04:51.591
I wasn't clever enough to sum 
it up like that, but yeah.

04:51.591 --> 04:53.321
Feeling a little more positive now?

04:53.631 --> 04:55.621
Well, I'm not sure about that.

04:56.141 --> 04:59.331
Your words are idealistic 
and lacking concreteness.

04:59.331 --> 05:01.121
Look, man...

05:01.121 --> 05:01.831
But...

05:03.861 --> 05:06.791
that's one thing,
and this is something else.

05:10.211 --> 05:11.381
Subaru, look!

05:11.381 --> 05:12.931
We found Reid's book!

05:13.281 --> 05:14.831
What?! For real?!

05:16.001 --> 05:18.891
It was Meili who found it. 
She did good, didn't she?

05:19.201 --> 05:23.841
I-It was nothing. I just 
happened to see it, that's all.

05:23.841 --> 05:25.071
Don't be silly!

05:25.071 --> 05:28.441
You should be proud of 
your own accomplishments!

05:28.441 --> 05:29.961
Well done, Meili!

05:29.961 --> 05:32.191
You're messing up my hair!

05:33.371 --> 05:36.951
Still, if you just found 
it by chance, then...

05:37.521 --> 05:42.701
It means we still haven't figured out 
how the archive works, unfortunately.

05:43.141 --> 05:46.621
There were other books I 
would've liked to find, too.

05:47.691 --> 05:49.381
Big Brother, you don't mean...

05:49.931 --> 05:55.091
I told you, I won't cut corners 
in ensuring you grow up healthy.

05:58.871 --> 06:03.441
So nobody's looked
at Reid's book yet, right?

06:03.441 --> 06:04.691
Obviously.

06:04.691 --> 06:09.151
We'd be in trouble if someone else read a 
book carelessly and lost their memories.

06:09.501 --> 06:14.651
Hey, we don't know for sure that it 
was the book that left me like this.

06:15.741 --> 06:18.151
This is gonna sound
really self-centered...

06:19.071 --> 06:21.711
but I think I'm the best 
choice for reading any books.

06:25.391 --> 06:26.291
Subaru...

06:29.411 --> 06:31.121
We're a team.

06:31.121 --> 06:35.001
Everyone has to take on some sort of 
role for the benefit of the group.

06:35.721 --> 06:37.471
Julius does the fighting.

06:37.951 --> 06:39.931
Foxidna's our intellectual.

06:39.931 --> 06:41.931
Ram's our verbal abuser.

06:41.931 --> 06:43.931
Meili's the cute one.

06:43.931 --> 06:45.931
Beatrice is also the cute one.

06:45.931 --> 06:48.271
Shaula does the gravure scenes.

06:48.591 --> 06:51.731
And Emilia-chan's the beautiful heroine.

06:51.731 --> 06:54.001
So this is a job for me.

06:54.001 --> 06:57.981
A lot of those
roles sounded kind of silly.

06:57.981 --> 06:59.731
That's not true!

06:59.731 --> 07:03.031
For your sake, Master... 
I'll take it all off!

07:03.031 --> 07:06.371
Actually, if you take off any 
more, it'll just scare me.

07:06.371 --> 07:07.631
You don't have to.

07:08.251 --> 07:10.711
I've been left high and dry!

07:11.011 --> 07:12.461
So anyway...

07:13.001 --> 07:16.051
No one objects to me reading the book?

07:18.721 --> 07:20.761
Make sure you come back to us.

07:20.761 --> 07:24.561
I won't call that a promise, though, 
because you'll just break it.

07:25.021 --> 07:27.231
If my memories get wiped,

07:27.231 --> 07:30.351
freeze me in ice and give 
me a good talking-to.

07:30.781 --> 07:34.181
No one would do anything 
that violent, I suppose!

07:34.181 --> 07:37.321
Yeah, I know. You're just too nice.

07:47.921 --> 07:48.871
Subaru...

07:49.381 --> 07:51.321
Okay, off I go!

07:51.321 --> 07:55.331
I might be home late, so you 
can have dinner without me.

07:56.801 --> 07:57.551
Dummy.

08:29.211 --> 08:30.461
Is this...

08:31.761 --> 08:33.581
Reid's memory?

08:34.031 --> 08:35.741
What's this?

08:35.741 --> 08:38.901
You're back again, mister?

08:43.281 --> 08:46.621
Who are you? Wait, where are we?

08:46.621 --> 08:48.471
Which should I ask first?

08:48.471 --> 08:51.381
Gosh, you're so greedy.

08:51.381 --> 08:53.181
But we don't dislike that.

08:53.181 --> 08:58.221
We just love greedy people, you know.

08:59.811 --> 09:04.621
This is the lonely white final 
resting place for souls,

09:04.621 --> 09:07.291
the cradle, Od Ragna.

09:07.291 --> 09:09.351
The corridor of memories.

09:14.451 --> 09:16.621
Corridor of... memories?

09:16.931 --> 09:20.091
Yeah, that's right!
The corridor of memories!

09:20.561 --> 09:26.831
And we are the Sin Archbishop in the 
Witch Cult representing Gluttony,

09:26.831 --> 09:28.021
Rui Arneb.

09:30.071 --> 09:33.101
It'll only be for a short time,

09:33.101 --> 09:36.391
but it's a real pleasure, mister!

09:38.851 --> 09:43.571
First of all, what the heck is a 
Witch Cult and a Sin Archawhatsit?

09:45.171 --> 09:50.951
The Witch Cult is a gathering of all 
the most hated people in this world.

09:51.361 --> 09:54.391
It does sound like the name 
of a band of evildoers.

09:54.391 --> 09:56.581
Which makes you an evildoer?

09:57.041 --> 10:02.801
You shouldn't be so mean to 
a sweet little girl, mister.

10:02.801 --> 10:05.351
We can get hurt, too, you know.

10:06.031 --> 10:11.661
You keep using "we." Is that supposed 
to be part of your character?

10:11.661 --> 10:12.521
Oh...

10:13.041 --> 10:14.861
You don't need to worry about that.

10:14.861 --> 10:17.341
We just have a few too many egos,

10:17.341 --> 10:21.021
so it's not really clear 
which one's in charge.

10:21.021 --> 10:23.731
It can't be helped, though.

10:25.251 --> 10:28.941
It's a gift from Big Brother 
and Brother Dearest.

10:28.941 --> 10:31.151
We ought to accept it.

10:31.151 --> 10:33.331
We'd be a failure as a 
little sister otherwise.

10:33.331 --> 10:36.671
Well, aren't you a cute little 
sister who loves her big brothers?

10:36.671 --> 10:38.661
I'm an only child, so I'm kinda jealous.

10:39.021 --> 10:44.101
Really? But you might have a 
little brother or sister by now.

10:44.101 --> 10:47.171
Don't say scary things like that! 
I don't even want to imagine it!

10:47.171 --> 10:49.961
We get it, mister.

10:50.721 --> 10:54.411
You feel like you've done your mom 
and dad wrong, don't you?

10:55.871 --> 10:58.591
You regret leaving without a word.

10:58.591 --> 11:02.981
You feel like you were 
a terrible son to them.

11:03.821 --> 11:05.831
How do we know that?

11:06.151 --> 11:08.531
Well, of course we do.

11:08.531 --> 11:17.161
Because there's no one who 
understands you better than we do!

11:17.621 --> 11:19.331
Don't touch me!

11:23.831 --> 11:29.861
We only want to give you 
some peace of mind, mister.

11:30.511 --> 11:33.311
Just what are you?
What are you getting at?

11:33.891 --> 11:37.011
All that about the cradle of Od 
Ragna, the corridor of memories...

11:37.011 --> 11:40.861
Nothing you say makes any damn sense!

11:45.091 --> 11:46.321
True.

11:46.591 --> 11:50.781
To sum it up, this is 
where souls are filtered.

11:51.161 --> 11:53.741
Where souls are... filtered?

11:54.101 --> 11:56.221
After you use a washrag,

11:56.221 --> 11:58.961
you wash it, dry it,
and use it again, right?

11:58.961 --> 12:01.141
It's the same for souls.

12:01.141 --> 12:03.601
The filth clinging to them is removed

12:03.601 --> 12:06.341
so they're all clean to use again.

12:06.341 --> 12:09.741
And is the "filth" clinging to it...

12:09.741 --> 12:12.051
stuff like memories and experiences?

12:12.051 --> 12:16.391
If that's the easiest way for 
you to understand it, sure!

12:16.391 --> 12:19.721
Think whatever you want!

12:19.721 --> 12:22.021
Memories and experiences are...

12:23.681 --> 12:24.771
filtered here?

12:29.301 --> 12:30.901
Then...

12:31.441 --> 12:36.951
were you the one who took my 
memories from before yesterday?

12:36.951 --> 12:38.081
That's right!

12:44.011 --> 12:45.921
Something's approaching the tower!

12:46.311 --> 12:48.751
Take care of Master!

12:54.171 --> 12:55.511
I'm going with her.

12:55.511 --> 12:57.261
Lady Emilia, let us go get Rem.

12:58.411 --> 13:00.491
Beatrice, stay with Subaru!

13:00.491 --> 13:02.311
Leave it to me, I suppose!

13:25.001 --> 13:26.461
Infinite...

13:34.261 --> 13:35.921
Hell's Snipe!

13:57.531 --> 13:58.731
No!

14:12.881 --> 14:15.381
It has been a while, Big Sister.

14:17.991 --> 14:22.551
In the end, this whole 
world runs on gluttony!

14:31.361 --> 14:35.531
So this means yesterday's
me came here, too.

14:35.921 --> 14:36.901
That's right.

14:37.401 --> 14:42.241
But it's so amazing, so 
wonderful, that you came back!

14:42.641 --> 14:46.161
How many times did it take 
for you to make it here?

14:47.401 --> 14:50.121
Come on, tell us, mister.

14:50.651 --> 14:53.461
We answered your questions.

14:53.461 --> 14:56.711
How many times does this make...

14:56.711 --> 14:59.471
after we ate you?

15:01.731 --> 15:03.211
That's...

15:04.961 --> 15:09.201
Don't worry. What happens in 
here doesn't make it outside.

15:09.201 --> 15:12.101
It's a secret just between you and us.

15:12.681 --> 15:15.571
Well, mister? How many times did it take?

15:17.881 --> 15:19.531
This is... the fifth time.

15:20.741 --> 15:23.431
Amazing! That's amazing! Just amazing!

15:23.431 --> 15:27.101
So amazing! Truly amazing! 
Absolutely amazing!

15:27.101 --> 15:29.931
So admirably amazing! And that's 
exactly what makes it...

15:29.931 --> 15:32.251
gluttony!

15:34.901 --> 15:41.011
We want to savor the taste of 
you until our stomach bursts!

15:41.371 --> 15:44.081
Based on our experience,

15:44.081 --> 15:47.221
we think appetite and
lust are very similar.

15:47.791 --> 15:50.931
And lust... means love, right?

15:50.931 --> 15:54.901
In other words, we love you, mister!

15:54.901 --> 15:57.481
Stop it!

16:00.191 --> 16:02.861
Give me back my memories or...

16:02.861 --> 16:04.161
You'll strangle us?

16:04.951 --> 16:08.491
You'll wring the neck of a 
frail little girl like us?

16:09.001 --> 16:12.551
You think you can actually do that?

16:12.551 --> 16:16.391
If that brings Subaru 
Natsuki's memories back,

16:16.391 --> 16:19.191
the man you are now will die, you know.

16:19.191 --> 16:19.821
Huh?

16:20.291 --> 16:21.891
Well, why wouldn't it?

16:21.891 --> 16:27.071
If those memories come back, who you are 
now will be overwritten and disappear.

16:27.071 --> 16:29.921
And that's the same as dying, right?

16:29.921 --> 16:34.391
Is bringing Subaru Natsuki 
back really worth all that?

16:34.391 --> 16:37.111
Wh-What horseshit are you spewing now?!

16:37.111 --> 16:39.571
Memories make people who they are.

16:40.901 --> 16:42.491
Mister...

16:43.571 --> 16:48.611
You have relationships that 
this version of you made.

16:51.481 --> 16:54.711
And maybe it's not right to say this...

16:55.431 --> 17:01.001
but Subaru Natsuki isn't exactly 
the ideal man, now, is he?

17:02.321 --> 17:04.691
Poor Emilia!

17:04.691 --> 17:07.921
Just because her birth was the 
same as that of the witch of old,

17:07.921 --> 17:10.611
everyone avoids her, the poor girl!

17:10.611 --> 17:15.021
How kind I am for still 
wanting to be by her side!

17:15.021 --> 17:17.211
And the weak, fragile Beatrice!

17:17.211 --> 17:23.901
That lonely little girl who spent all 
that time alone, with no one to rely on!

17:23.901 --> 17:28.641
I must be the one to take her by the 
hand down this dark, dangerous path!

17:28.641 --> 17:29.451
What are you...

17:29.451 --> 17:33.281
And Rem, who devoted all her love 
to you and got nothing in return!

17:33.281 --> 17:39.171
An incomplete being who tries to feel 
alive by desperately serving others!

17:39.171 --> 17:42.981
I have to be the one to lead her!

17:43.011 --> 17:44.741
What are you getting at?!

17:44.741 --> 17:48.631
We're just saying what 
Subaru Natsuki thought.

17:48.631 --> 17:51.371
What he wanted was always 
a sense of superiority.

17:51.371 --> 17:54.441
He had all those useful 
people waiting on him,

17:54.441 --> 17:57.521
and he got drunk on the pleasure of 
extending a helping hand to them.

17:57.521 --> 18:03.071
You really want to step aside for 
someone like that Subaru Natsuki?

18:05.271 --> 18:05.901
Well?

18:07.361 --> 18:09.321
Well? What'll it be?

18:09.321 --> 18:11.711
How about it? What will you do?

18:11.711 --> 18:14.591
You can do anything you want! 
Consequences be damned!

18:14.591 --> 18:16.661
Whatever you want to do, it's fine!

18:16.661 --> 18:20.041
No matter what you do, we'll forgive you!

18:20.461 --> 18:24.001
So what are you going to do, mister?

18:24.501 --> 18:28.181
Can you make such an important 
decision like this?

18:29.291 --> 18:36.271
Try loving yourself more seriously, 
more diligently, more genuinely!

18:49.401 --> 18:50.531
No...

18:52.201 --> 18:59.461
I want... to be with them... more...

18:59.461 --> 19:02.671
Uh-huh. We understand. Of course we do.

19:02.671 --> 19:05.211
We get it. We truly get it.

19:06.231 --> 19:07.321
No...

19:08.671 --> 19:09.871
No...

19:19.911 --> 19:20.861
No...

19:27.901 --> 19:28.841
No...

19:39.121 --> 19:40.091
No...

19:42.821 --> 19:44.041
I don't want this...

19:44.041 --> 19:47.021
Yes. That's right.

19:47.021 --> 19:50.051
So what do you think you should do?

19:51.291 --> 19:54.141
I'll... stay who I am...

19:54.141 --> 19:57.721
That's right. You'll stay who you are.

19:57.721 --> 19:59.691
You took it for yourself once.

19:59.691 --> 20:01.351
It's a game of musical chairs!

20:01.351 --> 20:05.061
The one who sits is the king!

20:05.061 --> 20:07.051
Now, acknowledge it!

20:07.051 --> 20:11.151
Subaru Natsuki is the stranger 
who's closest to you!

20:11.541 --> 20:12.861
So kill him!

20:12.861 --> 20:15.951
Kill him! Now, kill him!
You must kill him!

20:15.951 --> 20:20.161
Just kill him! Let's kill him!
Kill him off!

20:20.161 --> 20:22.641
Kill him for good!

20:22.641 --> 20:24.121
Subaru Natsuki...

20:24.121 --> 20:28.591
You are the one and only 
Subaru Natsuki in this world!

20:28.591 --> 20:30.761
You are no one's replacement!

20:45.751 --> 20:49.191
Did you get scared of me and decide 
to come out, Subaru Natsuki?!

20:50.001 --> 20:52.081
I don't want to disappear!

20:52.081 --> 20:53.821
I don't want to die!

20:53.821 --> 20:56.661
I want to stay with everyone!

20:56.661 --> 20:59.741
I love them all! So...

21:00.361 --> 21:03.441
So... I'm not you!

21:03.441 --> 21:05.221
You and I are...

21:05.221 --> 21:07.961
Who are you talking to, mister?

21:08.281 --> 21:10.921
There's no one here.
Who are you talking to?

21:23.581 --> 21:28.231
Why are you trying to 
choose one or the other?

21:41.451 --> 21:42.621
Stand up!

21:46.081 --> 21:47.041
Huh?

21:47.441 --> 21:48.751
Stand up!

21:49.341 --> 21:50.301
<i>Why...</i>

21:51.391 --> 21:54.761
<i>Why do you have to say that to me?</i>

21:54.761 --> 21:55.971
Stand up!

21:56.341 --> 21:57.741
<i>Who are you?</i>

21:58.351 --> 22:00.321
<i>Isn't this enough?</i>

22:00.321 --> 22:02.221
<i>I've agonized so much over this...</i>

22:02.221 --> 22:03.221
Stand up!

22:04.131 --> 22:07.701
<i>Even though it's so hard... so painful...</i>

22:08.631 --> 22:10.061
<i>Why?</i>

22:10.901 --> 22:14.731
Up! Up! Up! Stand up!

22:15.471 --> 22:16.441
<i>Why?</i>

22:17.001 --> 22:22.151
<i>Why... does my chest feel so hot?</i>

22:22.931 --> 22:25.251
Stand up, Subaru Natsuki!

22:27.681 --> 22:28.911
Stand up!

22:29.921 --> 22:31.331
My hero!

22:40.221 --> 22:43.641
If you're able to stand up, then go.

22:43.641 --> 22:46.681
Go and save all of them. All of it.

22:47.831 --> 22:51.651
All of... what? All of what?

22:51.651 --> 22:53.761
All of it means all of it.

22:53.761 --> 22:57.031
Everything. Everyone. Yourself...

22:57.581 --> 22:59.771
and the stranger who's closest to you!

23:02.171 --> 23:04.591
But can I do that?

23:04.591 --> 23:07.021
Do you seriously think I can?

23:09.481 --> 23:12.511
You can. Because...

23:12.511 --> 23:14.981
Because? Because why?!

23:14.981 --> 23:17.421
Help me! Answer me!

23:17.421 --> 23:19.571
In your own words... Tell me...

23:22.681 --> 23:23.971
You are...

23:26.681 --> 23:30.731
You are... my hero.

23:53.121 --> 23:54.251
Mister?

23:55.521 --> 23:57.461
What's wrong?

23:57.821 --> 24:00.111
Come on, let's continue with—

24:00.111 --> 24:02.011
You don't have to say any more.

24:04.831 --> 24:08.181
I've had enough of
your sick, twisted talk!

24:11.121 --> 24:13.331
Just one step...

24:13.331 --> 24:19.581
We were just one step away from tearing 
Subaru Natsuki and Subaru Natsuki apart!

24:19.581 --> 24:21.951
What the hell? Why would you try to—

24:21.951 --> 24:26.531
Because we can't eat the same 
person twice, obviously!

24:26.531 --> 24:29.281
We needed you to stay separate!

24:29.281 --> 24:35.751
The Subaru Natsuki we ate and the Subaru
Natsuki we didn't had to stay separate!

24:35.751 --> 24:37.501
What is it you guys want?

24:38.341 --> 24:40.711
To be happy.

24:40.711 --> 24:45.591
Tell me, mister, have you 
ever thought life was unfair?

24:45.591 --> 24:47.351
You can't choose where you're born.

24:47.351 --> 24:48.881
You can't choose your parents.

24:48.881 --> 24:50.621
You can't choose your surroundings.

24:50.621 --> 24:52.101
You can't choose your future.

24:52.101 --> 24:53.691
You can't choose anything.

24:54.021 --> 24:56.151
But what if you could?

24:57.111 --> 24:59.781
That's why we're searching

24:59.781 --> 25:04.081
for a rose-colored future that will 
make us glad we lived this life!

25:04.081 --> 25:07.241
And until we find that fateful life,

25:07.241 --> 25:11.371
we keep eating, keep biting, keep 
licking, keep sucking, keep devouring...

25:11.801 --> 25:14.121
keep gluttonizing!

25:14.541 --> 25:17.851
But no matter how many other 
people's memories we eat,

25:17.851 --> 25:21.091
we cannot obtain a memory of death.

25:21.091 --> 25:23.841
Tell us, what does it feel like to die?

25:23.841 --> 25:26.731
It must be painful, right?
Agonizing, right?

25:26.731 --> 25:29.101
Terrible, right? It hurts, right?

25:29.101 --> 25:31.771
Some people say it feels good!
Is that true?

25:31.771 --> 25:34.651
Tell me! Tell me!
Tell me, tell me, tell me!

25:34.651 --> 25:38.841
If you have my memories from 
yesterday, shouldn't you know that?

25:38.841 --> 25:41.211
But those are old, and they're not real!

25:41.211 --> 25:44.371
We want a fresher sensation!

25:44.371 --> 25:47.661
A juicy new frontier that 
no one else has ever known!

25:47.661 --> 25:52.331
A one-of-a-kind memory that no one 
else in this world can experience!

25:52.861 --> 25:57.401
The ease of being able to die and 
start over if you make a mistake!

25:57.401 --> 26:00.291
Even after you manage to 
find your perfect life,

26:00.291 --> 26:04.341
there's still a chance you'll 
mess up and ruin it all, right?

26:04.341 --> 26:08.301
But that's not the case for your life!

26:08.301 --> 26:10.181
So please...

26:10.511 --> 26:12.711
won't you let us...

26:15.231 --> 26:18.441
eat our fill of your life?

26:21.251 --> 26:25.181
My suffering, my death, and my life...

26:25.181 --> 26:26.901
all belong to me.

26:28.631 --> 26:32.391
I don't have a single damn 
thing to give to you!

26:32.391 --> 26:34.451
Just starve to death, you eat-and-runner!

26:35.841 --> 26:38.291
This isn't gonna go
the way you want it to.

26:39.411 --> 26:41.541
My name is Subaru Natsuki!

26:41.931 --> 26:45.941
Kenichi Natsuki and Nahoko 
Natsuki gave me that name.

26:45.941 --> 26:48.511
I'm not anything else. I'm me!

26:48.511 --> 26:51.791
Even though you might be 
overwritten and disappear?

26:51.791 --> 26:54.221
I'm gonna teach you some magic words.

26:54.641 --> 26:57.561
"That's one thing.
This is something else."

26:59.521 --> 27:03.421
Argh! We failed! We messed up!

27:03.421 --> 27:07.161
We goofed up! We screwed up! 
We botched it! We blew it!

27:07.811 --> 27:11.951
We'll just have to leave the rest to 
Big Brother and Brother Dearest...

27:12.421 --> 27:15.791
Your brothers are in this 
tower? I gotta move!

27:21.551 --> 27:22.481
What is this?

27:22.481 --> 27:24.311
The exit that leads out.

27:24.311 --> 27:25.921
What will you do, mister?

27:28.341 --> 27:29.761
You'll regret this.

27:30.151 --> 27:32.941
Big Brother and Brother 
Dearest have big appetites,

27:32.941 --> 27:34.721
and they'll do <i>anything</i> to satisfy them.

27:38.651 --> 27:41.601
It'll be fine. I remember our promise.

27:43.531 --> 27:46.311
I'm sure Subaru Natsuki 
would never forget it.

27:46.881 --> 27:47.691
So...

27:48.141 --> 27:49.961
I know we'll meet again.

27:49.961 --> 27:52.201
And next time, don't use the harsh voice.

27:52.201 --> 27:57.201
<b>Stand Up</b>

27:53.391 --> 27:55.511
Let me hear the gentle voice instead.

28:01.481 --> 28:03.121
Damn it all!

28:03.671 --> 28:05.601
I can't believe this guy!

28:05.601 --> 28:07.251
Stop it, Rui!

28:08.991 --> 28:11.471
What the hell are you doing?!

28:12.481 --> 28:14.851
What is this sensation?

28:14.851 --> 28:17.601
Dearness? When something feels dear?

28:17.601 --> 28:19.571
If it feels dear...

28:19.601 --> 28:21.351
Unforgivable!

28:21.351 --> 28:24.811
You will not escape! Never! Never!

28:32.251 --> 28:34.321
We threw away those pesky memories!

28:34.321 --> 28:37.541
All that's left is to eat you all up!

28:38.061 --> 28:42.831
Don't think this is over, Subaru Natsuki!

28:46.331 --> 28:48.291
Huh?! Wha—

28:52.821 --> 28:58.851
Your life belongs to us!
